    "interval": "Manifest start_unix through finish_unix, inclusive. Duration is monitor wall-clock elapsed time for the entire process, including setup and verification; it is not measured server-batch time.",
    "observations": "Receipt records whose time_unix falls within the inclusive manifest interval, retaining their original order. Event counts include start, sample, and finish. Maximum gap uses adjacent records including start/finish, not only sample events.",
    "quiet": "The receipt watcher quiet boolean must be true in every observation. This is sampled guest-host evidence, not proof of absence of all unobserved or hypervisor activity.",
    "sole_benchmark_lease": "Exactly one active lease line in every observation, with a constant ticket and a label beginning row-persistence-benchmark. Waiting lease requests are not active leases. Lean slot occupancy is checked separately.",
    "lean_ticket_changes": "No new_lean_ticket_since_sample flag is true, and the recorded lean_ticket_sequence is present and constant throughout the interval.",
    "heavy_processes": "The receipt watcher heavy_processes list is present and empty in every observation. This inherits the watcher process filter; it does not assert that no other processes existed.",
    "swap_pages": "End minus start /proc/vmstat pswpin and pswpout counters, system-wide pages. These cannot be attributed specifically to the benchmark. No byte conversion is made because the receipts do not record page size.",
    "cpu_jiffies": "End minus start aggregate cpu line from /proc/stat, in recorded USER_HZ accounting ticks and aggregated over logical CPUs. These are system-wide, not benchmark CPU time. guest overlaps user; guest_nice overlaps nice, so summing all ten fields double-counts guest time.",
    "steal": "The steal entry is the recorded aggregate /proc/stat steal counter delta, not a per-core or benchmark-specific elapsed duration.",
    "pass": "Conjunction of the explicitly listed checks. No numerical CPU, swap, or sampling-gap threshold is imposed; those observations remain visible rather than being described as zero activity."
